From: vphone <vphone@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 03:15:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] tu: Implement VK_EXT_fragment_shader_interlock

The hardware has no critical-section instruction. Vulkan defines the
interlock's order through rasterization order, which is per primitive in
primitive order. A pipeline with an interlock runs under SINGLE_PRIM_MODE
(FLUSH_PER_OVERLAP in GMEM, FLUSH_PER_OVERLAP_AND_OVERWRITE in sysmem),
which waits for an overlapping earlier primitive's pending work and
invalidates UCHE. Begin/end interlock are memory barriers so a critical
section's stores complete before the invocation does. An interlocked draw
is preceded by a wait for idle and cache invalidate so that the order
also holds across draws.

Not exposed before a7xx; shading-rate interlock is not implemented.

Generated-by: LLM
